    "title": "Why is April Fools' Day a thing? There are several historical ties",
    "text": "MICHIGANWho started April Fools Day? Possible origins, when to prank this weekSarah MooreLansing State JournalMarch 31, 2026, 10:46 a.m. ETSubscribe to hear this storyWatch your back this week, because April Fools' Day lands on Wednesday, April 1. People will soon dedicate 24 hours to plotting and pranking — behavior that may have started in 15th-century France or earlier.Whether it's a classic jump-scare, hiding fake bugs or handing out fake winning lottery tickets, April Fools' Day is a long-standing, unofficial international holiday that many people celebrate at home, in schools or at workplaces.",
